From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Ole Algoritme <olealgoritme@gmail.com>
Date: Sat, 17 Oct 2026 18:25:38 +0200
Subject: [PATCH] nvk: on Windows the driver build id includes the build's
 -Dnvk-build-id

Without an ELF build-id note, NVK on Windows identifies its build by the
Mesa version string and the timestamp of the module file.  That did not
tell driver packages apart: after a driver rollback, a game loaded
pipeline binaries another build had compiled from the disk cache, with
corrupted rendering.

The build id from -Dnvk-build-id (which the Windows build sets to a hash
of the patch series, the build options and the driver package version)
now goes into instance->driver_build_sha, so driverUUID, the disk cache's
driver id and the pipeline cache and shader binary UUIDs (which already
used NVK_BUILD_ID_OVERRIDE) all change with every build.
---
 src/nouveau/vulkan/nvk_instance.c | 13 +++++++++++--
 1 file changed, 11 insertions(+), 2 deletions(-)

diff --git a/src/nouveau/vulkan/nvk_instance.c b/src/nouveau/vulkan/nvk_instance.c
index 051aa26..3f24569 100644
--- a/src/nouveau/vulkan/nvk_instance.c
+++ b/src/nouveau/vulkan/nvk_instance.c
@@ -190,14 +190,23 @@ nvk_CreateInstance(const VkInstanceCreateInfo *pCreateInfo,
    STATIC_ASSERT(sizeof(instance->driver_build_sha) == BLAKE3_KEY_LEN);
    copy_build_id_to_sha1(instance->driver_build_sha, note);
 #else
-   /* No ELF build-id (Windows): the Mesa version plus what the OS says
-    * about the module this function lives in (its timestamp on Windows).
+   /* No ELF build-id (Windows): the Mesa version, the build id the build
+    * passes in (-Dnvk-build-id, a hash of the patch series, the build
+    * options and the driver package version), and what the OS says about
+    * the module this function lives in (its timestamp on Windows).  The
+    * build id is what keeps two builds from sharing pipeline caches and
+    * disk cache entries: the version string and the file time alone did
+    * not tell driver packages apart.
     */
    {
       static const char mesa_version[] = PACKAGE_VERSION MESA_GIT_SHA1;
       blake3_hasher blake3_ctx;
       _mesa_blake3_init(&blake3_ctx);
       _mesa_blake3_update(&blake3_ctx, mesa_version, strlen(mesa_version));
+#ifdef NVK_BUILD_ID_OVERRIDE
+      _mesa_blake3_update(&blake3_ctx, NVK_BUILD_ID_OVERRIDE,
+                          strlen(NVK_BUILD_ID_OVERRIDE));
+#endif
       if (!disk_cache_get_function_identifier(nvk_CreateInstance,
                                               &blake3_ctx)) {
          result = vk_errorf(NULL, VK_ERROR_INITIALIZATION_FAILED,
-- 
2.43.0

